  },
  question: "Is which compilation units an emitted stage0 crate depends on answered by ONE authority or by two? It is authored once in stage0_cross_unit_import_edges (the cross-unit grouping the partition folds into GeneratedPartitionCrateRow) and again by the units real Cargo.toml and lib.rs, which the derived reexport comparison in stage0_reexport_derivation_disagreements reads back against the authored edges. Equal intent at two sites is a reason to ask, not a finding: the reexports are established correct off this graph (the unit real manifest and lib.rs) and the authored edge list is what is missing them, so deriving the edges from the roster plus parsed imports plus the policy crate assignment dissolves the second authority rather than reconciling the two by hand. Until such a derivation exists the list stays authored grouping input, and that is the reconciliation this row keeps open.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "25f66b6a844dad438b1a3dcbaabf3619fb85026d",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.rust_crate_partition", decl_name: "stage0_cross_unit_import_edges") },
        tail: [CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "v2.workflow.rust_crate_partition", decl_name: "stage0_reexport_derivation_disagreements") }],
      },
      account: "Measured at revision 25f66b6a. Three derivation predicates were tried against the 93-row authored cross-unit import list and none reproduces it: raw parsed imports keep 84 of 93 and add about 156 import edges the list deliberately omits; a cross-crate-import predicate keeps 21 of 93 (keep 21, drop 72, add 0); a same-crate-import predicate keeps 63 of 93. The list is therefore grouping input the partition folds, not a view over imports, so there is no single authority yet. The twelve rows node stage0-crate-partition-covers-every-emitted-module added, to cover the previously uncovered emitted modules, equal the full parsed-import set for those twelve (62 authored rows equal 62 derived edges, symmetric difference empty in both directions), so their coverage is measured, not transcribed. NINE non-import edges remain authored with no import to derive. THREE are citable to a relation in the from-module and are kept with the citation: std_unicode_types to std_types at src/v2/workflow/rust_crate_partition.dag:572, cited to dag/std/unicode/types.dag:46 which uses std.types String with no import block; v1_compiler_parse to std_types at :625, cited to src/v1/02_parse.dag:46 and :118 which use String, List and NonEmptyStr without importing std.types; v1_compiler_infer_emit_info to v1_compiler_infer_items at :614, cited to src/v1/04_emit_info.dag:239 where ItemInfo is homed in infer_items and left un-imported to avoid a cycle. SIX are uncitable (the relation was grepped in the from-module and returned zero hits) and their owner owes a re-derivation from a real relation or a deletion: std_syntax to std_node at :544, dag/std/syntax.dag has no Node or std.node reference, zero hits, owner v2 std syntax; extdeps_uri to std_unicode_types at :565 and extdeps_uri to std_unicode_scalar at :566, dag/extdeps/uri.dag has zero unicode references, owner extdeps uri; v1_compiler_infer_types to v1_compiler_infer_items at :610 and v1_compiler_infer_env to v1_compiler_infer_items at :611, src/v1/04_types.dag and src/v1/04_env.dag have no InferItem or ItemInfo reference, zero hits, owner v1 compiler; v1_std_core to std_source_annotation at :603, src/v1/00_core.dag MissingAnnotation is a local variant not the std_source_annotation module, zero hits, owner v1 std core. RESIDUAL: the whole-population coverage admission still refuses 22 endpoints owned outside this node and outside this partition carrier, because neither module is rostered — 18 on v1_tests_claim_v1_source_chars_once_identity (owner node v1-source-chars-converted-once, gunbc#16910) and 4 on dry_run (owner adhoc-132254e5-c25). This node covers the twelve it owns; those two carry their own follow-ups and are named here so the stall is tracked, not remembered.",
